  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Use compound angle formulae to find the exact value of:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos105^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1-\\sqrt3}{2\\sqrt2}$",
          "worked": "Use $105^\\circ=60^\\circ+45^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\cos105^\\circ&=\\cos60^\\circ\\cos45^\\circ-\\sin60^\\circ\\sin45^\\circ\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot\\frac1{\\sqrt2}-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\cdot\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\\\&=\\frac{1-\\sqrt3}{2\\sqrt2}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\dfrac{13\\pi}{12}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1-\\sqrt3}{2\\sqrt2}$",
          "worked": "Use $\\dfrac{13\\pi}{12}=\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}+\\dfrac\\pi4$. Alternatively, convert to degrees: $195^\\circ=150^\\circ+45^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\frac{13\\pi}{12}&=\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\cos\\frac\\pi4+\\cos\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\sin\\frac\\pi4\\\\&=\\frac12\\cdot\\frac1{\\sqrt2}-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\cdot\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\\\&=\\frac{1-\\sqrt3}{2\\sqrt2}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q10-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cot285^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt3-2$",
          "worked": "Use $285^\\circ=240^\\circ+45^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\tan285^\\circ&=\\frac{\\tan240^\\circ+\\tan45^\\circ}{1-\\tan240^\\circ\\tan45^\\circ}\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt3+1}{1-\\sqrt3},\\\\\\cot285^\\circ&=\\frac{1-\\sqrt3}{\\sqrt3+1}\\\\&=\\frac{(1-\\sqrt3)(\\sqrt3-1)}{(\\sqrt3+1)(\\sqrt3-1)}\\\\&=\\sqrt3-2.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
  },
